            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a prospective groom, then the Tamil for consent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வரதட்சணை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வரதட்சணை — varataṭcaṇai — \"a dowry\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அவர்கள் வரதட்சணை வாங்காமல் திருமணம் செய்தார்கள். avarkaḷ varataṭcaṇai vāṅkāmal tirumaṇam ceytārkaḷ. They married without taking a dowry."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வரதட்சணை (varataṭcaṇai) வாங்கு, to take a dowry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வரதட்சணை (varataṭcaṇai) is borrowed from Sanskrit, built from vara, \"bridegroom\" (CDIAL 11309), and dakṣiṇā, \"a gift\" (CDIAL 6120); Tamil writes kṣ as ட்ச."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
