            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அவர் ஒரு மருத்துவரை மணந்தார். avar oru maruttuvarai maṇantār. He married a doctor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): மணந்தேன், maṇantēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Formal and literary; the everyday phrase is திருமணம் செய். The one married takes -ஐ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மண (maṇa) is native Dravidian (DEDR 4667). DEDR keeps மண \"to emit fragrance\" as a separate entry (4668)."
            }
          ]
